%S A006659 2,12,56,240,990,4004,16016,63648,251940,994840,3922512,15452320,
%T A006659 60843510,239519700,942871200,3711935040,14615744220,57562286760,
%U A006659 226760523600,893550621600,3522078700140,13887053160552
%N A006659 Number of closed meander systems of order n+1 with n components.
%C A006659 a(n) is the total number of long interior inclines in all Dyck (n+2)-paths. An incline is a maximal subpath of like steps (all Us or all Ds); interior means it does not start or end the path; long means of length >= 2. Example: for n=1, the 5 Dyck 3-paths are shown with long interior inclines in uppercase: uuuddd, uududd, udUUdd, ududud, uuDDud and so a(1)=2. - _David Callan_, Jul 03 2006
%C A006659 a(n) is the number of corners in all parallelogram polyominoes of semiperimeter n+3. - _Emeric Deutsch_, Oct 09 2008
%D A006659 N. J. A. Sloane and Simon Plouffe, The Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences, Academic Press, 1995 (includes this sequence).
%H A006659 Reinhard Zumkeller, <a href="/A006659/b006659.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1000</a>
%H A006659 Maylis Delest, Jean-Philippe Dubernard, and Isabelle Dutour, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1006/jsco.1995.1062">Parallelogram polyominoes and corners</a>, Journal of Symbolic Computation 20 (1995), nos. 5-6, 503-515.
%H A006659 Maylis Delest, Jean-Philippe Dubernard, and Isabelle Dutour, <a href="https://www.labri.fr/perso/maylis/ARTICLES.ps/JSC.ps.gz">Parallelogram polyominoes and corners</a>, 1995. (Author-hosted copy, compressed PostScript.)
%H A006659 Marie-Pierre Delest, Dominique Gouyou-Beauchamps, and Bernard Vauquelin, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01788555">Enumeration of parallelogram polyominoes with given bond and site perimeter</a>, Graphs and Combinatorics 3 (1987), 325-339.
%H A006659 Philippe Di Francesco, Olivier Golinelli, and Emmanuel Guitter, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/S0895-7177(97)00202-1">Meander, folding, and arch statistics</a>, Mathematical and Computer Modelling 26 (1997), nos. 8-10, 97-147.
%H A006659 Philippe Di Francesco, Olivier Golinelli, and Emmanuel Guitter, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9506030">Meander, Folding and Arch Statistics</a>, arXiv:hep-th/9506030, 1995.
%H A006659 Sergei K. Lando and Alexander K. Zvonkin, <a href="https://fpsac-archive.github.io/FPSAC91/ARTICLES/Lando_proc.pdf">Plane and projective meanders</a>, Proceedings of the 3rd International Conference on Formal Power Series and Algebraic Combinatorics (Bordeaux, 1991), 287-303.
%H A006659 Sergei K. Lando and Alexander K. Zvonkin, <a href="/A005316/a005316_1.pdf">Plane and projective meanders</a>, Séries Formelles et Combinatoire Algébrique, Université Bordeaux I, 1991, 287-303. (Annotated scanned copy.)
%H A006659 Sergei K. Lando and Alexander K. Zvonkin, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/0304-3975(93)90316-L">Plane and projective meanders</a>, Theoretical Computer Science 117 (1993), nos. 1-2, 227-241.
%H A006659 Sergei K. Lando and Alexander K. Zvonkin, <a href="https://www.labri.fr/perso/zvonkin/Research/proj-mean.pdf">Plane and projective meanders</a>, Theoretical Computer Science 117 (1993), 227-241. (Free copy hosted by the author.)
%H A006659 Simon Plouffe, <a href="/A000051/a000051_2.pdf">Approximations de séries génératrices et quelques conjectures</a>, Master's thesis, Université du Québec à Montréal, 1992. (OEIS-hosted copy.)
%H A006659 Simon Plouffe, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/0911.4975">Approximations of generating functions and a few conjectures</a>, Master's thesis, Université du Québec à Montréal, 1992; arXiv:0911.4975 [math.NT], 2009.
%F A006659 G.f.: 32/(sqrt(1-4x)*(1+sqrt(1-4x))^4).
%F A006659 a(n) = (n+1) * A002057(n-1). - _Ralf Stephan_, Aug 31 2003. Corrected by _Hunter Hogan_, Nov 13 2026.
%F A006659 a(n) = 2*binomial(2n+2, n-1). - _Emeric Deutsch_, Oct 09 2008
%F A006659 a(n) = {(-56 - 30*n - 4*n^2)*a(n+1) + (8*n+12+n^2)*a(n+2), a(0)=2, a(1)=12}. - _Simon Plouffe_ (master's thesis, 1992)
%F A006659 a(n) ~ 2^(2*n+3)/sqrt(n*Pi). - _Charles R Greathouse IV_, Dec 07 2011
%F A006659 E.g.f.: 4*exp(2*x)*(I_1(2*x) + x*(x - 1)*(I_0(2*x) + I_1(2*x)))/x^2, where I_n(x) is the modified Bessel function of the first kind. - _Stefano Spezia_, May 09 2022
%F A006659 From _Amiram Eldar_, May 15 2022: (Start)
%F A006659 Sum_{n>=1} 1/a(n) = 23/12 - 13*Pi/(18*sqrt(3)).
%F A006659 Sum_{n>=1} (-1)^(n+1)/a(n) = 53*log(phi)/(5*sqrt(5)) - 37/20, where phi is the golden ratio (A001622). (End)
%F A006659 a(n) = 2*A002694(n+1). - _Hunter Hogan_, Nov 13 2026
%p A006659 seq(2*binomial(2*n+2,n-1),n=1..22); # _Emeric Deutsch_, Oct 09 2008
%t A006659 f[x_] := 32/((1 + Sqrt[1 - 4x])^4*Sqrt[1 - 4x]); CoefficientList[ Series[ f[x], {x, 0, 21}], x] (* _Jean-François Alcover_, Dec 07 2011 *)
%t A006659 (* Alternative: *)
%t A006659 CoefficientList[Series[4*Exp[2x](BesselI[1,2*x]+ x(x-1)(BesselI[0,2x]+BesselI[1,2x]))/x^2,{x,0,22}],x]Table[n!,{n,0,22}] (* _Stefano Spezia_, May 10 2022 *)
%o A006659 (PARI) a(n)=2*binomial(2*n+2,n-1) \\ _Charles R Greathouse IV_, Dec 07 2011
%o A006659 (Haskell)
%o A006659 a006659 n = 2 * a007318' (2 * n + 2) (n - 1)
%o A006659 -- _Reinhard Zumkeller_, Jun 18 2012
%o A006659 (PARI) my(x='x+O('x^30)); Vec(32/(sqrt(1-4*x)*(1+sqrt(1-4*x))^4)) \\ _Altug Alkan_, Oct 14 2015
